## Mathematical disposition

The unique extension keeps the lattice covolume in the boundary/area estimate,
giving error `86V^(1/5)D^(4/5)+1` when `D>=max(1,V)`. Maximizing
`-delta/V+36D^(1/3)T delta^(1/3)` and choosing `T=(D/V)^(1/5)` supplies
the displayed constant, including a separate collinear case.

For a **full infinite** unit-separated periodic packing with `q` distinct
cosets, [finite Oler](../theory/03-oler-shell.md) on enlarging period
parallelograms proves `V>=q*sqrt(3)/2`. For `q<=D/16`, cells with
`V<=4q` then give population at most
`pi D^2/(2sqrt(3))+114q^(6/5)D^(4/5)+q`. For `V>4q`, a reduced
shortest-vector basis and exact row/column counts give a smaller bound.
Every actual source label is counted; separate coset hulls may differ.

Combining that candidate bound with the separate **unreviewed candidate**
linear global-minimizer reserve gives the conditional growing motif lower
bound. There is no theorem extracting a bounded motif from arbitrary
triangle-free minimizers and no Level I conclusion. Separation of a finite
crop, or of the individual infinite cosets, does not establish the required
cross-coset hypothesis. This distinction preserves the earlier 39-lattice
finite-union counterexample without contradiction.

Both the original checker and the repaired checker pass the earlier 16
crops/hulls, 309 sides and 18,154 lattice labels, plus four periodic patterns
with 5,462 labels, 214 coset-hull sides and 1,112 exact period/phase checks.
A quadratic-form lower bound covers all omitted period translates. The
repaired checker also rejects two individually separated but mutually too-close
cosets at their actual pair-distance check. These are finite regressions,
not certificates of global optimality or of the analytic infinite theorem.

## Activity, metadata and recovery

Fresh Asus inspection found the original working directory physically absent.
All eight retained Git metadata file hashes agree with the preserved snapshot;
there is no staged delta, metadata lock, or process cwd/fd reference to the
working path or its metadata. The initial three-member working archive and
the comprehensive six-member archive were freshly hash-verified. All three
ignored bytecode objects exactly recompile from their pinned original Git
sources under Python 3.14.7, with matching magic, original filenames and no
trailing marshalled data. They contain no additional unrepresented research.
Full original bytes and Git metadata are retained privately on both hosts.

The independent mathematical review gate protects PR956 and its source branch.
After this disposition lands, only the exact obsolete registration may be
retired under a repeated fresh activity/metadata/archive check and exact
preservation-head guard. Every other registration and all local branch refs
must remain unchanged. Retirement is recorded by a separate private execution
receipt; neither an absent directory nor this document alone authorizes bulk
pruning or establishes that deletion already occurred.
